title: Lists and tables
card: Chapter 5 | Lists and tables | Keeping many things together
say: One name can hold many values, in a list. A list keeps them in order.
uncard

new: lists.fathom
type:
  genesis:
    set shopping to a list of ("milk", "eggs")
    add "bread" to shopping
    scrawl "I need ", the size of shopping, " things: ", shopping
    for each thing in shopping:
      scrawl "- ", thing
    if shopping contains "eggs": scrawl "Don't drop the eggs!"
    scrawl "The first thing is ", item 1 of shopping, "."
  and the universe said i love you
zoom: lines 2-8
spot: line 2
say: A list of milk and eggs. The values go in brackets, with commas between them.
spot: line 3
say: Add bread to shopping puts bread at the end.
spot: line 4
say: The size of a list is how many things it holds.
spot: lines 5-6
say: For each thing in shopping goes through the list, one thing at a time.
spot: line 7
say: Contains asks if something is in the list.
spot: line 8
say: And item one of shopping is the first thing. Items are counted from one, the way people count.
spot: off
run
zoom: output
say: Three things, each on its own line, a warning about the eggs, and the first thing is milk.
wait
zoom: out

say: Items can be changed and taken out, too.
line: 8
type:

    set item 2 of shopping to "butter"
    remove item 1 from shopping
    scrawl shopping
zoom: lines 9-11
say: Set item two to butter changes the second thing. Remove item one takes the first thing out, so everything after it moves up.
zoom: out
run
zoom: output
say: Butter and bread.
wait
zoom: out

say: Lists of numbers can be sorted, added up, and more.
type:

    set scores to a list of (31, 7, 18, 25)
    scrawl sorted scores
    scrawl "Best: ", biggest of scores, ", average: ", average of scores
    scrawl first 2 of reversed scores
    scrawl join shopping with " and "
    scrawl "a,b,c" split by ","
zoom: lines 12-17
spot: line 13
say: Sorted gives a copy of the list, smallest first. The list itself stays as it was.
spot: line 14
say: Biggest of, smallest of, sum of and average of work a list of numbers out.
spot: line 15
say: Reversed turns it back to front, and first two takes the first two of those.
spot: lines 16-17
say: Join makes a list into one piece of text, and split by cuts text into a list.
spot: off
run
zoom: output
wait
zoom: out

card: Chapter 5 | Tables | Looking things up by name
say: A table is like a phone book. It keeps values under names, so you can look them up.
uncard
clear
type:
  genesis:
    set ages to a table of numbers
    set entry "Rex" of ages to 3
    set entry "Tom" of ages to 7
    scrawl "Rex is ", entry "Rex" of ages
    scrawl keys of ages
    if ages contains "Tom": scrawl "We know Tom."
  and the universe said i love you
zoom: lines 2-7
spot: line 2
say: A table of numbers starts empty.
spot: lines 3-4
say: Set entry Rex of ages to three keeps three under the name Rex. Setting it again would replace it.
spot: line 5
say: Entry Rex of ages looks it up.
spot: line 6
say: Keys of ages gives every name it holds, in alphabetical order.
spot: line 7
say: And contains asks whether a name is there.
spot: off
run
zoom: output
wait
zoom: out

say: Lists can hold lists, too. A list of lists of numbers is a grid.
line: 7
type:

    set grid to a list of lists of numbers
    add a list of (1, 2) to grid
    add a list of (3, 4) to grid
    scrawl grid, " / ", item 2 of item 1 of grid
zoom: lines 8-11
say: Item two of item one of grid reaches inside: the second number of the first row.
zoom: out
run
zoom: output
say: The rows are shown in brackets, and the number we reached for is two.
wait
zoom: out
